title: 'Fix validations failing for a session after a restart near a session change'
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    A validator restarted shortly before a session change could fail every backing and approval
    validation of the new session with `Session params unavailable (no active leaf?)` until the
    next session change.

    While at its in-flight task limit, candidate-validation dropped new leaves and fetched the new
    session's executor params at a block of the previous session. The runtime API cache then kept
    that empty answer for the whole session. Leaves are now applied at the task limit too, and a
    missing `SessionExecutorParams` result is no longer cached.
crates:
- name: polkadot-node-core-candidate-validation
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-node-core-runtime-api
  bump: patch
